Subject: [PATCH] Declare a static version in setup.cfg

backports.functools_lru_cache 1.6.6 declares its version only via
[tool.setuptools_scm] in pyproject.toml.  The AS windows-2025-msvc-builder
does not reliably run setuptools_scm's finalize_distribution_options hook
(infer_version), and that hook swallows its own exceptions, so the version
silently becomes None -> distutils get_version() returns "0.0.0" -> the wheel
is named backports.functools_lru_cache-0.0.0-*.whl and ActiveStateWheel
rejects it with "Distribution name and/or version could not be determined".
Neither shipping a PKG-INFO-bearing sdist nor SETUPTOOLS_SCM_PRETEND_VERSION
helps: both are read behind that same dead hook.

A static version in [metadata] is read by plain setuptools with no scm, no
toml and no builder cooperation.  Same fix as ActiveState/filelock PR #2.
Text-only patch (no rename headers) so every builder's applier handles it.

--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 [metadata]
 name = backports.functools_lru_cache
+version = 1.6.6
 author = Raymond Hettinger
 author_email = raymond.hettinger@gmail.com
 maintainer = Jason R. Coombs
